WEBVTT

00:06.940 --> 00:09.400
So they made it inside, did they?

00:09.830 --> 00:11.660
The legendary hero is inside!

00:11.660 --> 00:14.410
If you want to hunt him down,
return to the ruins!

00:14.410 --> 00:17.100
No way! They found Touka?!

00:17.100 --> 00:18.830
<i>We're safe for now.</i>

00:18.830 --> 00:20.820
<i>Distract them a little longer, would you?</i>

00:21.620 --> 00:23.230
Distract them...?

00:24.130 --> 00:24.940
Oh, no—

00:24.940 --> 00:27.870
No way! What is this stuff?!

00:29.630 --> 00:30.480
I'm staying here.

00:30.480 --> 00:31.050
Me too.

00:31.050 --> 00:32.590
I'm all over this!

00:31.050 --> 00:32.880
What the hell is with these guys?!

00:32.880 --> 00:35.100
<i>Devils are all such perverts!</i>

00:35.100 --> 00:36.050
In that case...

00:36.050 --> 00:38.010
I shall do my part!

00:38.010 --> 00:41.520
We've been charged
with distracting them, after all.

00:44.400 --> 00:46.450
<b><i>HE'S DEAD</i></b>

00:48.090 --> 00:50.270
Dead, dead, another day dead

00:50.270 --> 00:52.200
Head, arms, and legs gonna 
fall off any minute now

00:52.200 --> 00:54.330
Whole body hollowed out, dry as a desert...

00:54.330 --> 00:57.080
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

00:56.210 --> 00:57.100
<b>THE</b>

00:57.100 --> 00:57.640
<b>LEGEN</b>

00:57.640 --> 00:58.140
<b>DARY</b>

00:58.140 --> 00:58.600
<b>HERO</b>

00:58.600 --> 00:59.100
<b>IS</b>

00:59.060 --> 00:59.560
<b>DEAD</b>

01:03.930 --> 01:05.600
Spending every day like 
you're in a casket, trapped

01:05.600 --> 01:07.670
Ready for another night 
like the dead, collapsed

01:07.670 --> 01:09.420
Yeah, living like a carcass
 with just your "life" intact...

01:09.420 --> 01:11.710
Who wouldn't want a way 
to con themselves out of that?

01:11.710 --> 01:13.800
Breaking away from ideas of "should do"

01:13.800 --> 01:15.720
to live for yourself—
that's lots of fun, too...

01:15.720 --> 01:17.650
Otherwise you're just being a mark...

01:17.650 --> 01:18.760
And who wants that?

01:18.760 --> 01:22.270
You and I, we're just corpses

01:22.270 --> 01:26.540
Pawns of some faceless necromancer

01:26.540 --> 01:30.280
From one marionette to another, I say...

01:30.280 --> 01:36.450
How about we cut our strings together?

01:36.450 --> 01:37.250
Let's get dancing!

01:37.250 --> 01:39.290
Dead, dead, another day dead

01:39.290 --> 01:41.360
Head, arms, and legs gonna 
fall off any minute now

01:41.360 --> 01:43.380
Whole body hollowed out, dry as a desert...

01:43.380 --> 01:45.210
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

01:45.210 --> 01:47.270
Dead, dead, we're already dead

01:47.270 --> 01:49.300
Gonna shake off this 
mortal coil any minute now

01:49.300 --> 01:51.260
You just gotta laugh a life like this off!

01:51.260 --> 01:53.760
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

01:53.760 --> 01:57.600
I tell you, this world makes life so hard

01:57.600 --> 02:01.480
What can you do but dance 
the whole night through?

02:01.480 --> 02:04.740
Even if I collapse and my body decays

02:04.740 --> 02:09.520
that doesn't mean I'm rotten 
all the way down to my soul!

02:13.520 --> 02:15.940
<b>Episode 11</b>

02:13.520 --> 02:15.940
<b>The Legendary Hero Fights to the Death!</b>

02:17.670 --> 02:21.200
Hang on. That guy's your brother, Anri?

02:21.200 --> 02:22.280
Indeed.

02:23.010 --> 02:25.230
This is Friedrich Norstein.

02:25.230 --> 02:27.690
He's my elder brother.

02:27.690 --> 02:30.620
Anri, why have you chosen 
to side with the hero?

02:30.620 --> 02:32.340
Did he threaten you?

02:32.340 --> 02:35.710
I am traveling with Sir Touka 
of my own will.

02:35.710 --> 02:38.870
The purpose of my journey 
is to save the world.

02:38.870 --> 02:40.180
But why, Anri?!

02:40.510 --> 02:43.600
Have you forgotten what we 
went through three years ago?

02:43.600 --> 02:45.930
The pain they put us through?!

02:48.390 --> 02:49.970
Stop it.

02:49.970 --> 02:53.360
If you're Anri's brother, 
you know how stubborn she can be.

02:53.840 --> 02:56.500
She told me about the 
persecution you experienced.

02:56.500 --> 02:58.530
I get why you'd want revenge, too.

02:58.530 --> 03:01.920
But you need to stop dragging 
innocent people into it!

03:02.330 --> 03:05.380
My childhood friend, the people of Moaran...

03:05.380 --> 03:07.740
You've got nothing against them, do you?!

03:11.190 --> 03:15.530
It's true that I'd prefer 
not to harm the innocent.

03:15.530 --> 03:19.340
"Revenge" was merely a pretext under 
which to gain companions, after all.

03:19.340 --> 03:21.480
Revenge isn't your main goal?

03:21.480 --> 03:25.560
My goal is to depose
the royals, the nobility...

03:25.560 --> 03:27.680
All the ruling classes of the overworld.

03:27.680 --> 03:31.230
Then we'll bring it under necromancer control

03:31.230 --> 03:35.650
and remake it into a world where 
necromancers can live peacefully.

03:35.650 --> 03:38.690
There's nothing I won't do to achieve that.

03:38.690 --> 03:41.050
I do pity the people of Moaran,

03:41.050 --> 03:43.530
but they're a necessary sacrifice
to change the world.

03:43.530 --> 03:45.030
Give me a damn break!

03:45.030 --> 03:46.470
No matter what your reason is,

03:46.470 --> 03:48.190
no one'll kick back and accept that

03:48.190 --> 03:50.780
while you're killing off the people they love!

03:50.780 --> 03:52.080
Unfortunately...

03:52.650 --> 03:56.130
we necromancers have grown 
so accustomed to death

03:56.130 --> 03:59.000
that it's impossible for us to sympathize.

03:59.550 --> 04:03.180
You should free yourself
of obligation to the dead hero.

04:03.180 --> 04:05.650
How is the hero's death different

04:05.650 --> 04:07.930
than any of the countless deaths we saw in Hell?

04:07.930 --> 04:11.710
"The future of all outweighs a single death."

04:11.710 --> 04:17.050
As a necromancer yourself, 
you should be able to comprehend that.

04:18.630 --> 04:20.070
It's true...

04:20.070 --> 04:24.390
I did not shed a single tear 
upon the hero's death.

04:24.390 --> 04:29.220
As with the deaths of our many brethren, 
my sorrow dissipated immediately.

04:29.540 --> 04:30.700
But even so...

04:30.700 --> 04:35.210
the gratitude I feel for the hero, 
who saved me, remains!

04:35.210 --> 04:39.850
As does the promise I made to him!

04:40.500 --> 04:41.690
Promise?

04:42.230 --> 04:45.820
A promise so important that
you're now saving the world

04:45.820 --> 04:48.010
with the man who killed your benefactor?

04:48.010 --> 04:50.670
He didn't! It was just 
an unfortunate accident!

04:50.670 --> 04:52.810
Sir Touka did nothing wrong!

04:53.180 --> 04:54.100
Anri...

04:54.100 --> 04:56.220
Even though I dragged him into this,

04:56.220 --> 05:00.730
Sir Touka never complained!
He accompanied me, he saved me...

05:00.730 --> 05:03.070
I could never betray someone so kind!

05:03.970 --> 05:07.190
I love you, my brother, 
and my promise is important...

05:07.190 --> 05:10.530
But the path you walk is one of death.

05:10.530 --> 05:16.040
I care more for saving lives than taking them.

05:16.040 --> 05:18.770
That is why I travel to save this world.

05:18.770 --> 05:21.250
Why I choose the promise I made to the hero!

05:22.500 --> 05:24.340
Hey, look at you there!

05:24.340 --> 05:26.840
You're practically a snot fountain!

05:26.840 --> 05:30.310
If she won't do what you tell her,
 just kill her!

05:30.310 --> 05:33.690
A corpse can't betray you, after all.

05:37.330 --> 05:40.270
She really was worthless, wasn't she?

05:43.360 --> 05:44.740
Queen Adele?!

05:44.740 --> 05:46.100
No way...

05:46.100 --> 05:48.540
Damn, dude, thanks for killing her!

05:48.540 --> 05:49.700
Sir Diego!

05:49.700 --> 05:51.620
I absorbed her.

05:52.580 --> 05:56.230
Regeneration isn't the infernal 
generals' only power.

05:56.230 --> 05:59.130
They each have potent magic, too.

05:59.130 --> 06:01.510
Vertex has absorption magic,

06:01.510 --> 06:04.630
so the devil-conversion spell
 is still in effect.

06:04.630 --> 06:06.990
Now, it's time for the final game.

06:06.990 --> 06:10.090
If you wanna save those people, 
you have to slay <i>me</i>!

06:10.400 --> 06:13.800
Let's have a little fun, Touka Scott!

06:14.330 --> 06:18.080
Incredible! They all started chasing us
after we took off our clothes!

06:18.750 --> 06:22.370
You have a brilliant strategic 
mind... just like Touka!

06:22.370 --> 06:24.600
I'm not quite sure how I feel about that!

06:24.600 --> 06:25.940
Let's head to the mountains!

06:25.940 --> 06:30.090
Some of the traps Touka set three 
years ago should still be there!

06:30.090 --> 06:33.570
It appears many devils are 
heading to the ruins as well!

06:33.570 --> 06:36.290
Don't worry! Papa and the
others will handle them—

06:36.290 --> 06:37.020
Or not!

06:37.020 --> 06:39.380
Titties! Titties! Titties!

06:39.890 --> 06:43.180
Milly, I'll deal with this 
and head to the ruins!

06:43.180 --> 06:45.460
Hey... That's a cruel way to stop me.

06:57.910 --> 07:00.560
Damn it! "Fun game," my ass!

07:00.560 --> 07:03.480
I can't beat a damn Infernal General 
without the damn Sacred Sword!

07:04.900 --> 07:07.030
Don't run away now.

07:07.030 --> 07:11.110
I've been waiting <i>so</i> long to fight you!

07:11.110 --> 07:13.250
You guys took my Sacred Sword!

07:13.250 --> 07:15.280
We can't have a decent fight like that!

07:15.280 --> 07:18.000
If you really want a rematch with me,

07:18.000 --> 07:20.580
tell him to give me back the Sacred Sword.

07:20.980 --> 07:24.550
Then we'll have a proper duel—you and me.

07:24.550 --> 07:26.550
Fair and square.

07:26.550 --> 07:28.800
Fair and square?

07:28.800 --> 07:31.450
Yeah. You're cool with that, right?

07:31.450 --> 07:34.470
Or are you <i>afraid</i>
to go one-on-one with me?

07:35.680 --> 07:37.720
Don't fall for it, Diego!

07:37.720 --> 07:41.690
You've seen how he operates!
You must know he's plotting something!

07:41.690 --> 07:44.670
That's a nasty thing to say, Snot-Nose Bro.

07:44.670 --> 07:47.330
This is why Anri doesn't like you, you know.

07:47.940 --> 07:50.940
If I was gonna spring a trap on you,
 I'd have done it already.

07:50.940 --> 07:55.430
The Sacred Sword has a pin stuck 
in it that draws lightning, see?

07:56.660 --> 08:00.370
Draws lightning? The spell from Moaran, eh?

08:00.370 --> 08:05.330
Look, I'm pretty pissed off that you're trying 
to turn my childhood friend into a monster.

08:05.330 --> 08:09.300
The only thing that'll satisfy me
is busting you up in a duel.

08:11.120 --> 08:14.100
Go on, then. Give him back the sword.

08:14.100 --> 08:15.720
Have you lost your mind, Diego?!

08:15.720 --> 08:19.220
This is exactly what
I've been hoping for, really.

08:19.220 --> 08:21.340
I'd love to slay the hero in a duel

08:21.340 --> 08:24.190
and prove my strength!

08:24.190 --> 08:26.150
Then it's settled.

08:26.150 --> 08:28.760
We'll fight at the top of that tower.

08:28.760 --> 08:30.610
The Sacrificial Tower, eh?

08:30.980 --> 08:35.380
So one of us will wind up
a sacrifice this night.

08:35.380 --> 08:38.580
Won't the water god be <i>so</i> delighted?

08:38.580 --> 08:40.910
<i>Let's get to it, Diego.</i>

08:40.910 --> 08:42.210
I see.

08:42.210 --> 08:44.770
They're fighting it out atop the tower.

08:45.370 --> 08:49.840
Even if we have an alliance, 
I do dislike Diego...

08:49.840 --> 08:52.610
I've got no qualms
about taking my student's side.

09:00.010 --> 09:03.630
Sorry, but I've decided to possess Vertex.

09:03.630 --> 09:07.480
It's not much fun if I don't use 
everything at my disposal.

09:07.480 --> 09:09.880
You know that the Sacred Sword can nullify

09:09.880 --> 09:12.100
the Infernal Generals' 
regenerative powers, right?

09:12.540 --> 09:13.850
I don't mind.

09:13.850 --> 09:15.110
In fact...

09:15.110 --> 09:17.660
I appreciate the bigger target!

09:17.660 --> 09:18.530
<i>He dodged!</i>

09:18.530 --> 09:20.430
<i>He's faster than he looks!</i>

09:20.990 --> 09:22.450
Ein Rosabis...

09:24.120 --> 09:25.210
Touka!

09:24.120 --> 09:25.210
Sir Touka!

09:27.440 --> 09:30.270
Sorry, but I read you like a book just now.

09:30.270 --> 09:32.910
You're just an unremarkable 
villager at heart.

09:32.910 --> 09:36.880
Surely you didn't really 
think you could beat me!

09:36.880 --> 09:40.360
Are you actually under the delusion 
that you're the real hero now?!

09:41.070 --> 09:43.180
Nah, not for a second.

09:45.680 --> 09:50.150
You really thought I was gonna 
fight fair and square, dumbass?

09:50.500 --> 09:52.020
Damn you!

09:52.020 --> 09:54.730
You blew up the tower floor?!

09:55.990 --> 09:58.670
<i>I'll probably end up having to fight Diego.</i>

09:58.670 --> 10:00.780
<i>That's where you come in, Master.</i>

10:00.780 --> 10:03.030
<i>I'll give you our location via transceiver.</i>

10:03.030 --> 10:05.570
<i>Then you blow out the floor,
 drop him in the aqueduct...</i>

10:05.570 --> 10:08.130
<i>and hit him with all 
the lightning magic you can!</i>

10:08.130 --> 10:13.750
I can get all the zombies I control with 
remote necromancy to cast the same spell!

10:13.750 --> 10:18.570
I'll bet your regeneration's working overtime
to withstand a mass attack like this!

10:18.570 --> 10:22.120
Ethel's the one with the lightning spell?!

10:22.120 --> 10:26.270
You were bluffing this whole time,
Touka Scott?!

10:26.690 --> 10:29.480
I see. So <i>this</i> was your trap.

10:29.480 --> 10:33.440
But your mistake was 
failing to catch me in it.

10:34.400 --> 10:36.530
<i>Did the hero's body make it to you?</i>

10:36.530 --> 10:39.150
<i>That won't be enough to kill Friedrich.</i>

10:39.150 --> 10:42.370
<i>Possess the hero
and finish Diego off already.</i>

10:43.120 --> 10:45.550
<i>He should be pinned down at the moment.</i>

10:45.550 --> 10:47.080
<i>I can get him for sure!</i>

10:47.080 --> 10:49.040
<i>But just in case...</i>

10:50.000 --> 10:52.710
<i>I'm gonna hit him with max firepower!</i>

10:50.000 --> 10:52.710
<b>Touka's Mana Level: 9</b>

10:54.090 --> 10:56.420
It's time to end this...

10:56.420 --> 10:59.340
you Bloody Tears bastard!

11:06.730 --> 11:08.750
Looks like it worked.

11:10.940 --> 11:12.440
Now Yuna will—

11:12.870 --> 11:15.070
Huh? What happened to the tip?

11:16.730 --> 11:18.820
Touka! Are you all right?!

11:18.820 --> 11:21.570
Damn... What the hell was that?

11:22.900 --> 11:26.870
I thought you couldn't regenerate 
from attacks by the Sacred Sword!

11:26.870 --> 11:28.480
So sorry.

11:28.480 --> 11:32.870
Your attack never reached my body, you see.

11:32.870 --> 11:35.360
Like hell it didn't!

11:35.760 --> 11:38.380
Vertex has absorption magic.

11:38.380 --> 11:44.750
It's capable of absorbing any magical attack.

11:44.750 --> 11:46.910
The Sacred Sword is a magic weapon.

11:46.910 --> 11:50.780
No matter how many attacks
 you throw at me, I'll simply absorb them!

11:51.730 --> 11:53.820
You can't hit me from behind, either.

11:53.820 --> 11:56.520
I'll just channel everything
into my own mana.

11:57.010 --> 12:00.240
Then why didn't you absorb 
the lightning spells before?

12:00.240 --> 12:01.950
Oh, I didn't on purpose.

12:01.950 --> 12:06.530
I wanted to see what your 
plan was building up to.

12:06.530 --> 12:10.840
I like to pick the most fun option. 
It's just the kind of guy I am.

12:11.290 --> 12:13.860
I was so excited to see what you'd do,

12:13.860 --> 12:17.300
but you've even done me the favor 
of reverting to that form!

12:17.300 --> 12:21.330
It's a repeat of the battle three years ago
between the hero and the Infernal Generals!

12:21.330 --> 12:24.110
A development so thrilling, 
it's got me in tears!

12:25.810 --> 12:28.550
<i>He'll absorb any magic attacks I use.</i>

12:28.550 --> 12:31.820
<i>Damn it... How the hell do you beat this guy?</i>

12:31.820 --> 12:33.480
<i>Okay, man, calm down.</i>

12:33.860 --> 12:35.940
<i>There's gotta be a way.</i>

12:35.940 --> 12:39.020
<i>At the very least, I can try 
attacks that </i>aren't<i> magic!</i>

12:39.020 --> 12:42.460
Only the Sacred Sword can kill me!

12:42.460 --> 12:44.170
<i>Master, I'm clearing out for now!</i>

12:44.170 --> 12:45.580
<i>Gotta form a new plan!</i>

12:45.580 --> 12:47.030
Okay. Got it.

12:48.110 --> 12:49.500
Goodness me...

12:49.500 --> 12:52.020
I was really hoping you'd stay out of this.

12:53.610 --> 12:54.750
Sir Touka!

12:54.750 --> 12:56.370
Anri! Yuna!

12:56.370 --> 12:59.400
Is it true that he's absorbing 
the Sacred Sword's attacks?

12:59.400 --> 13:02.120
We heard the whole conversation 
over the transceiver!

13:02.120 --> 13:03.050
Yeah.

13:03.050 --> 13:05.330
But we're not outta the fight just yet.

13:05.330 --> 13:08.360
Sion the hero beat that thing 
three years ago.

13:08.360 --> 13:10.310
So there's gotta be a way!

13:10.310 --> 13:13.740
Anri, do you know how he did it?

13:14.800 --> 13:19.950
I fear I only met Sir Sion after 
he'd bested the Infernal Generals.

13:19.950 --> 13:22.440
But Miss Dorothy may know!

13:22.440 --> 13:24.560
Hey, Dorothy! You read me?

13:24.560 --> 13:27.930
<i>Zuzz... Zuzz...</i>

13:27.930 --> 13:29.460
What does "zuzz zuzz" mean?

13:29.460 --> 13:31.380
It must be some kind of code.

13:31.380 --> 13:33.910
I think she's just asleep!

13:33.910 --> 13:36.380
Damn it all! Why now, of all times?!

13:36.380 --> 13:37.370
Touka.

13:37.370 --> 13:40.510
I've seen that devil before.

13:41.780 --> 13:47.300
Three years ago, the hero defeated 
the Four Infernal Generals here in this city.

13:47.300 --> 13:50.580
Then you saw how he fought them?!

13:50.580 --> 13:54.390
Yeah. Though only from afar,
so I didn't see much.

13:54.780 --> 13:59.990
He split the sword into many tendrils,
so it was hard to tell which would strike.

13:59.990 --> 14:04.110
Maybe to keep the devil from reading 
the direction or timing of his attacks.

14:04.110 --> 14:07.640
Keep him from reading the direction 
or timing of attacks...

14:08.130 --> 14:09.280
<i>Sir Touka!</i>

14:09.820 --> 14:12.160
We've made it to a nearby cliff.

14:12.160 --> 14:13.180
What about you?

14:13.180 --> 14:15.290
<i>Hey, great timing!</i>

14:15.290 --> 14:16.830
<i>I got a favor to ask you!</i>

14:18.240 --> 14:19.620
Hey, hey, hey.

14:19.620 --> 14:21.710
This is supposed to be the big climax!

14:21.710 --> 14:24.090
We can't go back to a game of tag.

14:24.090 --> 14:27.670
You're the one who wanted 
a fair-and-square duel.

14:27.670 --> 14:29.540
Yeah, I am.

14:29.540 --> 14:31.720
And I'm done running now.

14:31.720 --> 14:33.090
Ein Eim...

14:35.190 --> 14:36.810
Exploding arrow!

14:38.310 --> 14:39.940
Damn it! Where'd that come from?!

14:39.940 --> 14:41.060
<i>Mana sight.</i>

14:42.000 --> 14:43.210
I knew it.

14:43.210 --> 14:46.740
You had no clue that was coming,
 so you couldn't block it.

14:46.740 --> 14:49.670
That absorption spell is more like a shield.

14:49.670 --> 14:51.950
It ain't covering your whole body.

14:51.950 --> 14:53.220
Now...

14:53.220 --> 14:55.910
I'll give you a nice taste 
of the Sacred Sword.

14:55.910 --> 14:58.450
You think you can hit me with it?

14:58.450 --> 15:00.420
I can use more than one shield, you know.

15:00.420 --> 15:02.380
I can also move them freely.

15:02.380 --> 15:04.930
Even if your mana sight 
lets you see my shields,

15:04.930 --> 15:06.840
you can't possibly hit me!

15:06.840 --> 15:08.150
<i>Form change...</i>

15:08.730 --> 15:09.700
<i>Worm!</i>

15:10.300 --> 15:12.760
I can still make a shield below me—

15:14.220 --> 15:16.720
How did you know I didn't 
have a shield there?!

15:16.720 --> 15:19.020
That should have been a blind spot for you!

15:19.020 --> 15:20.190
Sorry, man.

15:20.190 --> 15:23.420
I've got another set of eyes.

15:23.420 --> 15:26.800
<i>When I use mana sight while 
connected to Yuna via mana threads,</i>

15:26.800 --> 15:28.570
<i>she can use mana sight too.</i>

15:28.570 --> 15:32.120
<i>Plus, only I can see and hear Yuna.</i>

15:32.120 --> 15:33.190
<i>In other words...</i>

15:33.190 --> 15:34.910
Touka. The next one is...

15:34.910 --> 15:38.370
Right hip! Left shoulder! 
Left wrist! Right calf!

15:35.740 --> 15:38.370
<i>You'll never see these attacks coming!</i>

15:40.330 --> 15:43.240
Guess you'd better shield 
your whole body at once!

15:43.240 --> 15:46.800
Though if you did that, I bet it'd 
drain all your mana in no time!

15:49.710 --> 15:53.430
Well, this is even more 
entertaining than I expected.

15:53.760 --> 15:56.920
You can regenerate from 
Sacred Sword attacks after all?

15:56.920 --> 15:59.960
Yeah, because I'm possessing a corpse.

15:59.960 --> 16:02.580
Even if the Infernal General's 
regeneration is nullified,

16:02.580 --> 16:04.920
my necromantic regeneration isn't.

16:04.920 --> 16:06.230
I see.

16:06.610 --> 16:11.710
Then I should be able to beat you by 
destroying a zombie's weak point—the head.

16:12.490 --> 16:14.610
Yes, I suppose.

16:14.610 --> 16:17.330
But it won't be that easy to hit him there.

16:17.330 --> 16:19.840
It's the place he'll be 
keeping the most guarded.

16:19.840 --> 16:21.080
In that case...

16:21.080 --> 16:25.320
I just need to wear down his mana 
by forcing constant regeneration

16:25.320 --> 16:28.040
until he reveals his weak point!

16:28.040 --> 16:31.460
<i>Milly will surely reach Touka soon.</i>

16:31.460 --> 16:33.880
<i>Until then, I'll support him!</i>

16:33.880 --> 16:36.290
I can't let you interfere any longer.

16:37.220 --> 16:40.680
I'd really rather not fight you, you know!

16:41.080 --> 16:43.770
We've got an alliance, don't we?

16:43.770 --> 16:45.450
I could say the same thing!

16:45.450 --> 16:47.510
Why did you try to kill Diego?!

16:48.150 --> 16:50.700
He'll drag you down someday!

16:50.700 --> 16:54.030
We're better off ditching 
that dead weight now!

16:54.030 --> 16:56.950
I can't lose any more of my brethren!

16:58.990 --> 17:01.370
Why are you so damned stubborn?!

17:07.500 --> 17:10.000
A war of mana attrition, eh?

17:10.000 --> 17:11.390
How amusing!

17:11.390 --> 17:13.470
As befitting a battle between zombies!

17:14.210 --> 17:16.090
I dunno if I'd put amusement first right now.

17:16.090 --> 17:19.300
Your shields have shrunk an awful lot.

17:19.300 --> 17:21.560
That's what makes this so fun!

17:21.560 --> 17:26.550
I'm so happy to be reduced 
to this state, I'm in tears!

17:26.550 --> 17:29.020
Got a masochism fetish, huh?

17:29.020 --> 17:34.080
Life in Hell was a constant battle
against the devils for survival.

17:34.080 --> 17:37.980
I just don't feel alive without
that kind of thrill!

17:37.980 --> 17:41.470
And that's the revenge I want on humanity.

17:41.470 --> 17:46.630
I want to plunge this peace-addled world 
into death and madness once more

17:46.630 --> 17:48.460
to make it like Hell!

17:48.460 --> 17:49.630
Give me a damn break!

17:49.630 --> 17:53.720
Don't drag us into your weird fantasy!

17:54.920 --> 17:59.010
Someday you'll all understand how I feel!

17:59.010 --> 18:03.480
You'll be having so much fun, you'll be 
breathing your gratitude to me in tears!

18:03.480 --> 18:05.430
The hell I will!

18:05.430 --> 18:07.390
Sorry, but my dream

18:07.390 --> 18:10.360
is a slow life with a pretty 
girl with hot thighs!

18:14.260 --> 18:15.390
Touka!

18:16.110 --> 18:17.380
Sir Touka!

18:20.140 --> 18:21.780
<i>Talk about terrible timing.</i>

18:22.140 --> 18:24.740
<i>The side effect of the soma drops...</i>

18:24.740 --> 18:27.990
Hey, now... Why'd you just fall over?

18:27.990 --> 18:30.180
We're only getting started!

18:31.030 --> 18:33.130
Still, what luck.

18:33.130 --> 18:35.670
Looks like the cavalry's here...

18:37.590 --> 18:39.630
<i>My</i> cavalry, that is!

18:39.630 --> 18:42.870
Guess it's game over for you!

18:44.010 --> 18:45.040
<i>Not yet...</i>

18:45.040 --> 18:46.720
<i>It's not over yet!</i>

18:51.150 --> 18:52.370
Now <i>that</i> was close.

18:52.370 --> 18:53.610
I let my guard down!

18:55.650 --> 18:57.030
Sir Touka!

18:55.650 --> 18:57.030
Touka!

18:57.030 --> 18:59.170
I'm crying here!

18:59.170 --> 19:03.660
You don't have enough mana 
left to pierce my head!

19:03.660 --> 19:06.340
Looks like this really is the end.

19:07.290 --> 19:08.400
<i>Actually...</i>

19:09.050 --> 19:11.750
<i>I've got one vial of soma drops left.</i>

19:11.750 --> 19:12.620
Don't do it!

19:12.620 --> 19:16.670
It's the soma drops that have you 
collapsing and coughing up blood, right?

19:16.670 --> 19:18.230
Hey, come on.

19:18.230 --> 19:20.480
I just need to get my mana back.

19:20.480 --> 19:21.790
<i>Your</i> mana?

19:21.790 --> 19:24.200
You remember what
your real mana level is, right?

19:24.200 --> 19:27.580
You used a vial of soma drops last night
to take over my body,

19:27.580 --> 19:29.830
and you've used four since then!

19:29.830 --> 19:31.410
Any more than that and...

19:31.410 --> 19:34.220
You got any better ideas?

19:34.220 --> 19:38.050
Can you find out where the 
Bloody Tears jerk stashed his body?

19:38.050 --> 19:40.550
Or do you want to take my place, Anri?

19:40.550 --> 19:44.910
If I switch souls at my current mana level,
 I'll degenerate for sure.

19:45.660 --> 19:48.620
This is the only way.

19:48.960 --> 19:50.490
Don't worry.

19:50.490 --> 19:53.580
I've managed to luck my way through so far.

19:53.580 --> 19:55.540
I'll do it again now.

20:00.630 --> 20:02.010
See?

20:02.010 --> 20:03.220
All right...

20:03.220 --> 20:05.840
Now that his guard's down, this is my chance!

20:06.230 --> 20:07.720
Let's finish—

20:07.970 --> 20:09.680
Touka!

20:07.970 --> 20:09.680
Sir Touka!

20:09.680 --> 20:13.140
Hey, c'mon now! You can't just self-destruct!

20:13.140 --> 20:15.060
Sir Touka! Speak to me!

20:15.060 --> 20:16.270
Touka?!

20:16.270 --> 20:22.140
It's anticlimactic if you don't
 fight to the bitter end!

20:22.140 --> 20:26.740
It can't end here!
Anri, you take over the hero role!

20:27.550 --> 20:29.490
Do you require my aid...

20:32.740 --> 20:34.520
impostor hero and comrades?

20:36.460 --> 20:39.070
I guess they can't hear me.

20:41.380 --> 20:44.210
<i>If I use possession necromancy 
on him in this state,</i>

20:44.210 --> 20:47.350
<i>Sir Touka's soul will surely break down.</i>

20:47.350 --> 20:49.760
<i>But with so little time left,</i>

20:49.760 --> 20:53.810
<i>the best path would be for me 
to take over the hero's body and fight.</i>

20:53.810 --> 20:58.770
<i>Sir Touka would surely prefer 
that I save Dame Yuna as well.</i>

20:59.460 --> 21:02.460
<i>I've gotten over so many deaths.</i>

21:02.460 --> 21:06.410
<i>I'll get over losing Sir Touka, too.</i>

21:08.410 --> 21:10.810
<i>Wait, what am I thinking?!</i>

21:10.810 --> 21:13.370
<i>Sir Touka is still alive!</i>

21:13.700 --> 21:15.520
<i>If he's still alive...</i>

21:16.460 --> 21:17.570
Dame Yuna.

21:17.570 --> 21:20.120
I hope that you can hear my voice.

21:21.100 --> 21:22.840
I'm sorry, Dame Yuna.

21:23.300 --> 21:26.240
I cannot yet abandon Sir Touka.

21:26.240 --> 21:29.970
I want to wager every second I have
on him regaining consciousness!

21:30.440 --> 21:31.760
So...

21:31.760 --> 21:32.960
It's okay.

21:32.960 --> 21:35.060
I feel the same way.

21:35.720 --> 21:37.200
Ein Seil!

21:37.200 --> 21:39.310
I'll buy us time.

21:39.310 --> 21:42.280
I'd say that's my job!

21:46.490 --> 21:53.450
My revenge will be most anticlimactic 
if Touka doesn't wake up first.

21:53.450 --> 21:55.160
Who the hell are you?

21:55.160 --> 21:57.510
You don't know me?

21:57.510 --> 22:00.750
My goodness. 
You're disqualified from existence.

22:00.750 --> 22:02.870
Kyle Ozment...

22:00.750 --> 22:07.720
<b>Kyle Ozment
Former Companion of the Hero; Effectively a God</b>

22:02.870 --> 22:06.960
Former companion of 
the hero and effectively a god.

22:07.720 --> 22:09.970
<b>15 minutes until Yuna and the others become devils</b>

22:10.010 --> 22:21.060
<b>Next Time</b>

22:10.290 --> 22:12.890
"Fine, just for you..."

22:11.030 --> 22:21.060
<b>The Legendary Hero Is a Duo!</b>

22:12.890 --> 22:15.920
Honey Honey Honey Honey

22:15.920 --> 22:20.290
Hi, Honey Honey Trap Trap

22:21.440 --> 22:26.580
Hey, I've got a melty marshmallow secret

22:27.910 --> 22:31.780
It's just bursting with sugar, you know...

22:31.780 --> 22:37.100
Hey, I know you want a taste... don't you?

22:38.190 --> 22:42.130
Don't bother to hide it, it's clear as day...

22:42.130 --> 22:44.880
Come a little closer, now

22:44.880 --> 22:48.940
A fleeting glimpse of lusty pink

22:48.940 --> 22:52.050
A seductive voice with a hint of danger

22:52.050 --> 22:57.640
See? I've already got you under my spell...

23:00.690 --> 23:04.160
It's a true-true-true hazard to pursue

23:04.160 --> 23:07.940
This sweetest trap of romance

23:07.940 --> 23:10.750
So cu-cu-cu-cute how you'll fall in love...

23:10.750 --> 23:13.660
In this literal pit I dug!

23:14.550 --> 23:17.790
You can't shoo-shoo-shoo me 
away when I pursue

23:17.790 --> 23:21.650
Such intense romance needs a strategy

23:21.650 --> 23:25.820
I'll kee-kee-kee-keep on 
setting bait every day...

23:26.540 --> 23:28.340
In my honey trap

23:28.340 --> 23:31.330
Honey Honey Honey Honey

23:31.330 --> 23:35.660
Hi, Honey Honey Trap Trap
